  "title": "Stopping-expression runtime evaluation semantics (CNL-0076)",
  "description": "JSON Schema for a halt-decision record under CouncilSpec v2. Evaluation cadence is end-of-round only. Expressions MUST be side-effect free; impure ASTs are rejected before any round. Intra-round true-then-false flaps do not halt: only the frozen end-of-round snapshot is visible to the evaluator. SUCCESS:CNL-0076",
  "unit_id": "CNL-0076",
  "state": "SUCCESS",
  "sentinel": "SUCCESS:CNL-0076",
  "completion_sentinel": "SUCCESS:CNL-0076",
  "title_human": "Stopping-expression runtime evaluation semantics",
  "question": "At what cadence is a stopping expression evaluated (mid-turn, end-of-turn, end-of-round), must it be side-effect free, and what happens when a predicate becomes true and then false again before the round ends?",
  "depends_on": [
    "CNL-0010"
  ],
  "dependency_note": "CNL-0010 owns surface grammar and static unsatisfiability. Its artifact is absent on this worktree. This unit specifies runtime evaluation over a closed typed AST that a CNL-0010 parser would emit. Grammar gaps do not block cadence, purity, or flap rules.",
  "produced_by": {
    "vendor": "cursor",
    "model": "grok-4.6",
    "role": "council-systems-designer",
    "execution_substrate": "headless-linux"
  },
  "catalog_anchor": {
    "path": "command-center/WORK-UNIT-CATALOG.json",
    "line": 38048,
    "snippet": "\"id\": \"CNL-0076\""
  },
  "answers": {
    "cadence": "end-of-round",
    "mid_turn": "FORBIDDEN",
    "end_of_turn": "SNAPSHOT-UPDATE-ONLY-NO-HALT",
    "side_effect_free": true,
    "purity_enforcement": "bind-time-reject",
    "flapping_rule": "sample-at-end-of-round-no-latch",
    "unknown_does_not_halt": true,
    "floors_seam": "halt_eligible = (result is true) AND floors_met; floors are CNL-0077. This unit's fixtures treat floors_met as true.",
    "rationale": {
      "why_not_mid_turn": "A mid-turn sample would halt on a speaker's in-progress metric write before the turn ledger closes, making halt order-dependent on tool-call interleaving inside one seat.",
      "why_not_end_of_turn": "End-of-turn halt would skip remaining seats in the round. Speaker order would change whether a flap is observed. CNL-0077 floors (every mandated role having spoken) cannot be stated if halt is allowed between seats of one round.",
      "why_sample_not_latch": "Latch-on-true requires observing intra-round values. This unit forbids those observations as evaluation events. Sampling the frozen end-of-round snapshot is the unique deterministic function of the round's closing metrics.",
      "why_reject_effects": "A mutating term would make AND/OR evaluation order observable. Rejecting effects makes order irrelevant and keeps the snapshot frozen. Purity is a gate, not a hope."
    }
  },
